From f85709b0a7ddcec75ebdfc69c87682e0f81e918e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Glathe <jens.glathe@oldschoolsolutions.biz>
Date: Sun, 31 May 2026 21:54:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kbuild: dtbinst: mark __dtbs_install as .NOTPARALLEL to avoid
 install -D race
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The dtbs_install target invokes multiple parallel 'install -D -m 0644'
commands (one per .dtb) that all write into the same vendor
subdirectories (qcom/, allwinner/, actions/, etc.).

GNU coreutils 'install -D' performs a non-atomic "check + mkdir"
sequence. When many jobs race to create the same parent directory,
some of them fail with:

    install: cannot create directory '.../device-tree/actions'

This latent race has existed for years but becomes much more visible
on distributions that default to high parallelism (Ubuntu 24.04/26.04
etc.) and ship large numbers of vendor device trees.

Add .NOTPARALLEL for the __dtbs_install target. This forces only the
install rules to run serially while leaving the rest of the kernel
build fully parallel. The performance impact is negligible — DTB
installation is tiny compared to compilation.

Signed-off-by: Jens Glathe <jens.glathe@oldschoolsolutions.biz>
---
 scripts/Makefile.dtbinst | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/scripts/Makefile.dtbinst b/scripts/Makefile.dtbinst
index 9d92041..3de271b 100644
--- a/scripts/Makefile.dtbinst
+++ b/scripts/Makefile.dtbinst
@@ -40,4 +40,6 @@ endif # CONFIG_ARCH_WANT_FLAT_DTB_INSTALL
 __dtbs_install: $(addprefix $(dst)/, $(dtbs))
 	@:
 
+.NOTPARALLEL: __dtbs_install
+
 .PHONY: $(PHONY)
-- 
2.53.0

